# Phase 5 STOP-LATE-EVENT: a turn held mid-stream (working), stopped with
# Ctrl-C and a second prompt typed in the same read as the stop, so the
# prompt is in hand before the stopped turn has ended. fx v0.0.16 queues
# such a prompt at once and shows nothing of its turn until its worker
# takes it: idle, the Cancelled frame, the window title from the stopped
# turn, working, then the frame with the prompt -- working ahead of the
# frame that shows its Thinking. xfx's runtime sends the stopped turn's end
# and the prompt's start with no wait between, so its UI mostly reads them
# in one drain. Then done, and the exit clears the record.
gateway p5-lifecycle-osc-interruptnext-turns.json
xfx: env XFX_SOUND=off
wait 4
type first question
key Enter
held
wire s00-working
key C-c s e c o n d Space q u e s t i o n Enter
release
held
wire s01-second
release
wait 2
wire s02-done
keep
type /quit
key Enter
wait 2
wire s03-exit
